WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.340
- My favorite teacher,
I had, I was lucky too.

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.920
I had about three or four
that really impacted my life.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.940
But I would say the one
that impacted me most

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.020
was my drama teacher from high school.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.600
His name was Christopher
Hasket and his nickname is Kit.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.020
He still lives in Orlando.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:17.930
And he was the first
teacher that when I said

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.039
I wanted to be a stand-up
comic and an actor.

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:22.720
Oh, what a great shot, I
don't know how you guys got-

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:26.073
- Yeah, we do our homework, Billy.

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:31.040
- You know, he was the first
teacher that took me seriously.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.420
And I think the good teachers know

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.141
that sometimes all the
kids don't quite fit into

00:00:36.141 --> 00:00:38.290
the rest of the group.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.900
And that maybe some kids
need to be connected with

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.850
on a different level.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:45.480
And, you know, he was the
first real adult teacher

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.940
that took me serious
in what I wanted to do.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:49.950
You know, I wanted to be
a comedian and an actor.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.920
And I told some of my teachers that,

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.380
and you know, they had me pegged

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:55.150
for ending up working at a Chevron.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.850
And that's okay, that
would have been okay too.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.360
But he was the teacher
that said, you know man,

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:02.500
if you really want to do this,
it's not enough to dream it.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.750
You have to put your time in.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:04.970
You have to put your work in.

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:07.350
And then I had to do my senior year over

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.930
and I only had three or four classes

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.760
that second senior year.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:14.690
And told me, he said,
instead of going home

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:16.960
or screwing off or taking a nap,

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.420
he said, come to the auditorium

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:19.830
and learn to build sets with me.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.730
And let's talk about, let's
talk about what it takes.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:25.150
Let's talk about New York,
Chicago, Los Angeles.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.780
Let's talk about what
you want to go after.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:29.610
Let's talk about television,
film, theater, Broadway.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.260
And he just had an impact,

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:33.000
not only educationally on my life,

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.150
but talking to me
seriously and then saying,

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:39.430
yeah you can do this, but
I'm not going to lie to you

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:41.410
there's so much work involved.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.020
So you have to take it seriously.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.250
Take your fun seriously,
is what he would say to me.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:47.190
Take your fun seriously.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.980
And he just had a huge impact in my life

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:51.022
and I will love him forever for that.

00:01:51.022 --> 00:01:52.280
I really will.

